-- title:
--   Terminal and descendant displacement defects
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. An ordered tree has finite levels $0,1,2,\dots$ with a single root, and monotone surjective parent maps from level $k+1$ to level $k$; edge weights are positive and sum to $1$ over the children of each parent. Each node carries a nonexpansive selfmap of $K$, and the tree is evaluated bottom-up: a node's value is its map applied to the weighted average of its children's values. Fix a tree evaluation and a common point $b$.
--
--   1. **Terminal defect.** $\sum_{d<N}\sum_{v\text{ at level }d}\|f_{d,v}(b)-b\|$, the unweighted displacement of all maps strictly above depth $N$.
--   2. **Descendant level defect.** For a node $v$ at level $k$ and a level $d\ge k$,
--   $$
--   \sum_{s\text{ desc. of }v\text{ at level }d}\pi(s)\,\|f_{d,s}(b)-b\| ,
--   $$
--   and $0$ for $d<k$.
--   3. **Internal descendant defect.** The sum of the descendant level defects over $d<N$. It bounds the error transmitted to the root when a subtree is replaced by the common point.
-- source:
